@startuml Web-CMS
' Web CMS base model for LessHeadCMS
' Layers: Website (global) -> Page (tree) -> Block (in an area) -> Content (channel-neutral)
' Rule: the CMS knows roles (Area), not positions ("top left"). Layout is up to the frontend.
' Multilingual: standard pattern (enum Language + self-reference "translation of" + {unique}), with {translations}:
' "Übersetzung anlegen" (create translation) copies a page with its blocks into another language.
'
' Adapt per project/design:
'  - adapt the enums Template and Area to the layout of the frontend
'  - add/remove block types: class XyBlock extends Block { ... } + Page *-- "n" XyBlock : on
' Composition (*--, diamond at the whole): blocks, tiles, FAQ items and nav items are parts of their whole -
' they are created, ordered and edited in the form of the whole and deleted with it.
'  - add content types: class Xy extends Content { ... } + "translation of" relationship ({translations}) + value in enum ContentType
' Several websites in one CMS: see the comment block "Multiple websites" at the end.

' ============================================================
' Value ranges
' ============================================================

enum Language {
  DE
  EN
}

enum NavLocation {
  MAIN
  FOOTER
  META
}

enum Template {
  STANDARD
  WITH_SIDEBAR
  LANDING_PAGE
}

' Areas of a page. Header and footer are global (Website / Navigation), not per page.
enum Area {
  HERO
  MAIN
  SIDEBAR
  BEFORE_FOOTER
}

enum ContentType {
  POST
  EVENT
  SERVICE
}

enum ListSort {
  NEWEST_FIRST
  OLDEST_FIRST
  ALPHABETICAL
}

' ============================================================
' Website: global settings, navigation
' ============================================================

package "Website" {

  ' Exactly one record per website. Language-neutral.
  class Website {
    + name: string {title}
    + base_url: string {pattern: url}
    + logo: media?
    + copyright: string?
    -- SEO defaults --
    + default_meta_description: text? {maxLength: 160}
    + default_share_image: media?
  }

  ' One navigation per location and language
  class Navigation {
    + name: string {title}
    + location: NavLocation {unique}
    + language: Language {unique}
  }

  ' Internal (Page) or external (URL)
  class NavItem {
    + label: string {title}
    + external_url: string? {pattern: url}
    + position: sort {by: Navigation, NavItem}
  }
}

' ============================================================
' Pages: tree, route, meta
' ============================================================

package "Pages" {

  ' Every language version is a page of its own; translations point at their original.
  class Page {
    + title: string {title}
    + slug: string {pattern: slug}
    + language: Language {unique}
    + template: Template
    + position: sort {by: "child of"}
    + published: visibility
    -- SEO --
    + seo_title: string? {maxLength: 60}
    + meta_description: text? {maxLength: 160}
    + share_image: media?
    + noindex: bool
  }
}

' ============================================================
' Blocks: the content elements of a page
' All block types of a page share one order (sort via the abstract class).
' The frontend groups by area and keeps the order.
' Blocks have no language of their own: they belong to the language version of their page.
' ============================================================

package "Blocks" {

  abstract class Block {
    + name: string {title}
    + area: Area
    + position: sort {by: "on"}
    + anchor: string? {pattern: slug}
    + published: visibility
  }

  class HeroBlock extends Block {
    + heading: string
    + subheading: text?
    + image: media?
    -- Button --
    + button_text: string?
    + button_url: string? {pattern: url}
  }

  ' Running text, optionally with image and link
  class TextBlock extends Block {
    + heading: string?
    + body: richtext
    + image: media?
    + link_url: string? {pattern: url}
  }

  ' One image = list with one element, several = gallery/slider
  class ImageBlock extends Block {
    + title: string?
    + images: media(ImageMeta)
  }

  class CtaBlock extends Block {
    + statement: string
    + button_text: string
    + button_url: string? {pattern: url}
  }

  class FaqBlock extends Block {
    + heading: string?
  }

  class FaqItem {
    + question: string {title}
    + answer: richtext
    + position: sort {by: FaqBlock}
  }

  ' Image tiles with link (teasers on pages)
  class TileBlock extends Block {
    + title: string?
  }

  class Tile {
    + label: string {title}
    + image: media
    + external_url: string? {pattern: url}
    + position: sort {by: TileBlock}
  }

  ' Dynamic list: "the 3 newest posts of category X"
  class ListBlock extends Block {
    + heading: string?
    + content_type: ContentType
    + item_count: int {min: 1, max: 50}
    + sort_order: ListSort
  }

  ' Embeds shared content (e.g. a contact box on many pages)
  class SnippetBlock extends Block {
  }
}

' Additional data per image in ImageBlock.images
class ImageMeta <<media_meta>> {
  + caption: string?
}

' ============================================================
' Content: channel-neutral data, not tied to a page
' ============================================================

package "Content" {

  abstract class Content {
    + title: string {title}
    + slug: string {pattern: slug}
    + language: Language {unique}
    + teaser: text? {maxLength: 300}
    + image: media?
    + published: visibility
  }

  class Post extends Content {
    + published_on: date
    + body: richtext
  }

  class Event extends Content {
    + starts_on: date
    + ends_on: date?
    + location: string?
    + description: richtext?
  }

  class Service extends Content {
    + description: richtext
    + price: decimal?
  }

  class Person {
    + name: string {title}
    + job_title: string?
    + email: string? {pattern: email}
    + photo: media?
    + bio: richtext?
  }

  class Category {
    + name: string {title}
    + slug: string {pattern: slug}
    + language: Language {unique}
  }

  class Snippet {
    + title: string {title}
    + language: Language {unique}
    + body: richtext
    + image: media?
  }
}

' ============================================================
' Relationships
' ============================================================

' Website
Website "n" --> "0..1" Page : home page

' Navigation
Navigation *-- "n" NavItem : belongs to
NavItem "n" --> "0..1" NavItem : child of {cascade}
NavItem "n" --> "0..1" Page : links to

' Page tree and language versions
Page "n" --> "0..1" Page : child of
Page "n" --> "0..1" Page : translation of {translations} {cascade} {unique}

' Blocks are parts of their page (relationships are not inherited, hence one per block type)
Page *-- "n" HeroBlock : on
Page *-- "n" TextBlock : on
Page *-- "n" ImageBlock : on
Page *-- "n" CtaBlock : on
Page *-- "n" FaqBlock : on
Page *-- "n" TileBlock : on
Page *-- "n" ListBlock : on
Page *-- "n" SnippetBlock : on

' Internal link targets (alternative to the external URL)
HeroBlock "n" --> "0..1" Page : button target
TextBlock "n" --> "0..1" Page : link target
CtaBlock "n" --> "0..1" Page : button target
Tile "n" --> "0..1" Page : links to

' Repeating groups
FaqBlock *-- "1..*" FaqItem : belongs to
TileBlock *-- "1..*" Tile : belongs to

' Blocks that show content
ListBlock "n" --> "0..1" Category : filtered by
SnippetBlock "n" --> "1" Snippet : shows

' Language versions of the content (relationships are not inherited, hence one per class)
Post "n" --> "0..1" Post : translation of {translations} {cascade} {unique}
Event "n" --> "0..1" Event : translation of {translations} {cascade} {unique}
Service "n" --> "0..1" Service : translation of {translations} {cascade} {unique}
Category "n" --> "0..1" Category : translation of {translations} {cascade} {unique}
Snippet "n" --> "0..1" Snippet : translation of {translations} {cascade} {unique}

' Content among itself
Post "n" --> "0..1" Category : belongs to {filter_by:language}
Post "n" --> "0..1" Person : written by
Event "n" --> "0..1" Category : belongs to {filter_by:language}
Service "n" --> "0..1" Category : belongs to {filter_by:language}

' ============================================================
' Multiple websites (documentation only - the model above is the standard case with ONE website)
' ============================================================
' Standard: one website. Pages and navigations belong to no website; Website has exactly one record.
' For several websites in one CMS, use the existing means. The lines below are valid as they are once the leading
' quote is removed (see templates/web-cms.md, "Multiple websites"):
'
' 1. Pages and navigations become parts of their website - add:
'
'Website *-- "n" Page : belongs to {unique: slug_per_site}
'Website *-- "n" Navigation : belongs to {unique}
'
' 2. Order per website and parent page, slug unique per website and language - in class Page, replace the lines
'    position, slug and language with:
'
'    + position: sort {by: "belongs to", "child of"}
'    + slug: string {pattern: slug} {unique: slug_per_site}
'    + language: Language {unique} {unique: slug_per_site}
'
' 3. Navigation: the {unique} on "belongs to" (line above) puts the new relationship into the {unique} group of
'    Navigation -> one navigation per location, language and website.
'
' 4. Page: its {unique} group (language + "translation of") stays as it is - it defines the language versions, and
'    {translations} allows nothing else in it. The named group slug_per_site (slug + language + "belongs to") comes on
'    top: the same slug may occur in every website and language, but only once per website and language. A translation
'    is created in the website of its original ("Übersetzung anlegen" copies the relationship); its new language keeps
'    the slug free.
'
' 5. Content types (Post, Event, Service, Category, Snippet) can stay shared across the websites, or each gets its own
'    composition (e.g. Website *-- "n" Post : belongs to) - a project decision.
'
' Migration: switching later, existing pages and navigations must be assigned to a website - "Änderungen prüfen"
' (check changes) asks for a backfill value (the id of an existing website). If two existing pages share slug and
' language, the new group slug_per_site blocks the change with a list of the rows until the duplicates are cleaned up.

@enduml
